ightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice. 1 paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab way unchanged.\n\nProposal is resource alignment audit to apply logging only where mandatory. Still treats compliance as logging practice, just selective. Introduces process of audit? Probably paradigm preserving? It is standard compliance classification. Might be slightly paradigm stretching introduces new elements tools/processes but still treats compliance as logging practice => 2. Could be 1 = standard compliance and logging practice; lab way unchanged. Audit is maybe common.\n\nI think paradigm_relatedness = 1? The description: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way of working is unchanged. Actually audit changes allocation, but still treats compliance as separate logging requirement. Might be slightly paradigm stretching introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice => 2.\n\nI'll choose 2.\n\nOriginality: degree not only rare but ingenious... 4 = not expressed before AND ingenious. 3 = unusual interesting shows some imagination. 2 = interesting. 1 = common mundane boring.\n\nPortfolio audit to avoid over-engineering is fairly common, mundane. Probably 1 = common, mundane, boring.\n\nEvidence: Risk-tier triage and selective compliance spending is a routine project governance practice.\n\nScore 1.\n\nApplicability: degree idea clearly applies to stated problem. 4 solves identified problem directly related. Problem: AI R&D lab must decide how to respond how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Proposal addresses allocating funding for necessary compliance upgrades only where mandatory. That's directly applicable to meeting logging mandate with resource constraints. So 4? Solves identified problem that is directly related: do X to get Y, Y is part of stated problem. Yes.\n\nScore 4.\n\nEffectiveness: degree will so