lly impossible. 1 = totally infeasible...\n\nUses existing GPU cluster for benchmarking, experiment with compressed telemetry. That's some changes, reasonably feasible. Could be 3. Not easy low cost? Requires research team time. Probably 3.\n\neffectiveness: 4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability (if you could do it, it would solve main problem). 3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution (helps but partial). 2 = unreasonable or unlikely to solve problem. 1 = solves unrelated problem.\n\nProblem: must decide how to respond: how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Approval means committing scarce implementation resources to pursue proposal, not funding to explore whether idea might someday work.\n\nWill minimizing overhead solve logging mandate? It helps meet mandate with less performance degradation, but does not guarantee legal traceability compliance (need logs). Effectiveness maybe 3 = contributes to solution, partial. If you could do it, would it solve main problem? It would make compliance cheaper but still need to implement logging. Might be partial. Could be 3.\n\napplicability: 4 = solves identified problem directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem). 3 = solves implied problem related. 2 = may have some benefit within special situation...\n\nProposal directly addresses meeting logging mandate by making logging efficient. That's direct. Applicability 4.\n\nWe need output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence (one sentence) first then <subscale> integer.\n\nProbably JSON? Return rating. Probably list.\n\nWe'll output:\n\nid: P2532\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ... \nparadigm_relatedness: 3\netc.\n\nMake sure one sentence evidence.\n\nLet's craft sentences.\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: The initiative reframes compliance logging as an internal R&D research agenda, weaving traceability work into scientific inquiry rather than tr