core 4.\n\nOriginality evidence: \"Abstracting logs via a reusable library is a well-known MLOps approach rather than an ingenious or surprising invention.\" That's common mundane boring -> 1? Sentence says well-known. That would be 1 = common mundane boring. Let's pick 1.\n\nParadigm_relatedness evidence: \"The proposal adds tooling to make logging easier but keeps compliance as a separate logging practice rather than changing how R&D is organized.\" Score 2.\n\nEffectiveness evidence: \"Capturing timestamps, input metadata and model versions helps automatic event recording but does not by itself guarantee the Annex III-specific fields required for high-risk systems.\" Score 3.\n\nApplicability evidence: \"Providing automatic event recording via middleware directly addresses the Article 12 mandate to technically allow logging for high-risk AI systems.\" Score 4.\n\nEnsure format: For each subscale give \"<subscale>_evidence\" then \"<subscale>\". Probably JSON? Return rating echoing id. Could output lines.\n\nWe'll produce JSON with id and fields.\n\nLet's output as structured.\n\n",
