 = reasonable and will contribute to solution of problem (helps, but only partial). Could be 3. Not full solve logging mandate, just capacity.\n\nApplicability (1-4): degree clearly applies to stated problem.\nSolves identified problem directly related? Logging mandate requires technical ability to record events over lifetime. Storage needed. That's directly related. Level 4 = solves an identified problem that is directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem). Yes storage for logs is part. So 4.\n\nParadigm_relatedness (1-4): degree preserves/modifies paradigm.\nDefinitions: 4 paradigm breaking introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 paradigm stretching changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners...)\n2 slightly paradigm stretching introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 paradigm preserving standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way unchanged\n\nThis is just infrastructure audit for logs. Still treats compliance as logging practice. Introduces new elements? tiered cold storage is a tool/process but still compliance as logging practice. Might be slightly paradigm stretching = 2. Or paradigm preserving =1? Standard compliance practice is to ensure storage capacity. That's standard. Hmm.\n\nIt says strategic review of storage... implement tiered cold-storage architecture. That's a new element but still treats compliance as logging practice. So 2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. Yes.\n\nOriginality (1-4): degree rare but ingenious.\nCommon, mundane, boring =1. This is common infrastructure audit. So 1.\n\nNeed output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>.\n\nProbably JSON? The instruction says return rating echoing its id. Could be list.\n\nI'll produce:\n\nid: P2105\nimplementability_evidence: ...\nimplementability: 3\netc.\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence for each.\n\nLet's craft sentences.\n\nImplementability evidence: Assessing disk capacity and deploying tiered cold storage with budget adjustment is a reasonably feasible IT project for an R&D lab. Score 3.\n\nAcceptability evidence: Capacity audits and archival budgeting are common, norm-compliant business practices that raise no legal or social concerns. Score 4.\n\nEffectiveness evidence: Securing storage prevents resource contention but does not by itself ensure logs capture the specific events required by Article 12(2)-(3). Score 3.\n\nApplicability evidence: Long-term log storage directly addresses the lifetime logging mandate in Article 12(1) and Recital 71. Score 4.\n\nParadigm_relatedness evidence: The proposal adds storage tools and processes while keeping compliance as separate logging practice without changing how R&D is conducted. Score 2.\n\nOriginality evidence: Infrastructure capacity audits for regulatory data retention are a common, mundane operational response. Score 1.\n\nReturn.\n\n",
