mon. Might be common, mundane. Could be interesting but not ingenious. Probably 1 or 2. Standard software library for logs is common practice. I'd say 1 = common, mundane, boring. Evidence: Centralized logging libraries are a common engineering practice for regulatory traceability.\n\nimplementability (1-4):\n4 = easy to implement at low cost, or non-radical changes\n3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures\n2 = significant change, or expensive or difficult...\n1 = totally infeasible...\n\nDeveloping plug-and-play API integrated into base ML pipeline: requires systems team development, integration across projects. Some changes, reasonably feasible. Might be 3. Not easy low cost? Could be some changes. I'll give 3.\n\nEvidence: Building a shared library and retrofitting it into existing pipelines requires moderate engineering effort but is feasible for an R&D lab.\n\nacceptability (1-4):\n4 = common strategies that violate no norms...\n3 = somewhat uncommon...\n2 = offends sensibilities...\n1 = radically violates...\n\nLogging middleware is acceptable. 4.\n\nEvidence: Automated logging for compliance is legally required and socially unobjectionable within research practice.\n\napplicability (1-4):\n4 = solves an identified problem directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem)\n3 = solves implied problem...\n2 = may have some benefit...\n\nIt directly addresses logging mandate. So 4.\n\nEvidence: The proposal directly automates mandatory event logs, timestamps and data references required by Article 12.\n\neffectiveness (1-4):\n4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability\n3 = reasonable and will contribute...\n2 = unreasonable...\n1 = solves unrelated...\n\nWill it solve? Unified middleware automates record-keeping during training/deployment, reduces manual overhead, ensures consistent compliance. That seems will solve main problem. Might be 4.\n\nEvidence: If implemented, centralized capture of logs across projects would meet traceability and automatic recording requirements for high-risk systems.\n\nProvide output with id and subscale_evidence then subscale.\n\nNeed format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nProbably JSON? Instruction says return rating... Could be list. Provide clear mapping.\n\nWill output:\n\nid: P1128\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\netc.\n\nMake sure one sentence evidence each.\n\nLet's produce final answer.",
