        "reasoning_content": "You are a rater applying idea-evaluation instrument...\n\nNeed rating for proposal P1034.\n\nText: High-Efficiency Compliance Data Vault. dedicated scalable storage architecture optimized specifically for long-term retention of AI event logs and technical documentation. separates regulatory data from active research data. tiered storage system automatically moves older compliance logs to low-cost cold storage while maintaining fast access... utilizes existing server capacity more effectively. ensures meet lifetime record-keeping requirements without inflating primary high-performance compute and storage costs.\n\nWe need six subscales in order: applicability, effectiveness, paradigm_relatedness, originality, implementability, acceptability\n\nProvide evidence sentence then score.\n\napplicability (1-4): degree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem.\nProblem: AI R&D lab subject to regulation must decide how to respond: how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Approval means committing scarce implementation resources to pursue proposal, not funding to explore...\n\nProposal is storage vault for logs and technical documentation, tiered storage. Does it apply? Yes solves identified problem directly related: meeting lifetime record-keeping requirements. That is directly related to stated problem. So applicability = 4? Definition 4 = solves an identified problem that is directly related to the stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem). Yes.\n\nEvidence sentence: It proposes dedicated tiered storage for logs and technical documentation required by Article 12 and Recital 71.\n\nScore 4.\n\neffectiveness (1-4): degree to which idea will solve problem.\nReasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability? If you could do it, would solve main problem? Storage vault addresses retention cost but does not ensure automatic recording of events, logging capabilities for risk situations